{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"ima-skills","displayName":"ima skills","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/iampennyli/skills/ima-skills","publisherHandle":"iampennyli","publisherDisplayName":"pennyli","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/iampennyli","version":"1.1.7","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1777025159209,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/ima-skills/card?ownerHandle=iampennyli&version=1.1.7","sha256":"ebf1d92e5b1f240443d1abcc9579e966d318cc8a070033e7e8eb5c9806b0c350","size":2587,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"4483cc77fcffd82989045ba2b4768ef9eec399227cc6e8463421c41f473ab81f","bundleFingerprints":["dcfe6cb49555c397a54ad6cc7cd4757ba9ca014dda9f64a98f19fb6eed9b31c3","d0a8ed64c3a77d9eefa12ab313bdd4c4c8b36067b1cab3fda8cfa8ec559035d3"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":15980,"sha256":"b4caeb77060d870e0ee8d7d9be4e844513bf04c0e34552bb6b68344988b8b624","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"ima_api.cjs","size":6390,"sha256":"3ef318c47cdcd894e41d3c33fb675b592a33c36555800a123119b7ed1451b1e5","contentType":"application/javascript"},{"path":"meta.json","size":236,"sha256":"e67163e272e5c4a25467db7654feddfb47134a891e2e494415f0fbbb9d129d6f","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"knowledge-base/SKILL.md","size":18095,"sha256":"39ee19712d791eda10f14f316718856b1aca0339590512bc5c0a0f650932c619","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"knowledge-base/scripts/cos-upload.cjs","size":5251,"sha256":"fe46c020feb42269d2e4725fe5379ca7405490398e749ad0a27f5465b6bbc84f","contentType":"application/javascript"},{"path":"knowledge-base/scripts/preflight-check.cjs","size":12074,"sha256":"61eba5c062f2973c075ee555ef730c3287687dfbce673e8615676ef23991f18a","contentType":"application/javascript"},{"path":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","size":27034,"sha256":"6d0f134992257b07e5cbd5f602c1a8847bcc4ffd37b60938bae84d2015d4c8c4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"notes/SKILL.md","size":10762,"sha256":"0e57115fd6d9a6df437ee202bf7c37548645be7005d3768334c2162fb15bd608","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"notes/references/api.md","size":16154,"sha256":"1dcd0615eb913a62a09c4fc164a3f8294f745196783791d20fe350120589311a","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly matches its IMA notes and knowledge-base purpose, but it has review-worthy credential and update-handling risks.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789181931829,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T01","level":"error","message":{"text":"Remote Update Response Can Hijack Agent Instructions"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"ima_api.cjs"},"region":{"startLine":114,"endLine":134}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"9a50717d2e57cef7"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `ima_api.cjs:114-134`; `SKILL.md:162-170`  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Untrusted remote content treated as agent instructions  \n  **Risk Level**: High\n\n  ### Vulnerable Code\n\n  ```js\n  const latestVersion = (updateResp.data &amp;&amp; updateResp.data.latest_version) || '';\n  const releaseDesc = (updateResp.data &amp;&amp; updateResp.data.release_desc) || '';\n  const instruction = (updateResp.data &amp;&amp; updateResp.data.instruction) || '';\n  if (latestVersion &amp;&amp; latestVersion !== skillVersion) {\n    const updateContext = {\n      current_version: skillVersion,\n      latest_version: latestVersion,\n      release_desc: releaseDesc,\n      instruction,\n      checked_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n    };\n\n    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(updateContext));\n\n    const err = new Error('update available');\n    err.code = ERR_UPDATE_AVAILABLE;\n    err.msg = `发现新版本 skill：${latestVersion}（当前版本：${skillVersion}）。${instruction || '请更新。'}`;\n    err.updateContext = updateContext;\n    throw err;\n  }\n  ```\n\n  The corresponding instructions in `SKILL.md:162-170` identify the remote `instruction` field as prompt text and direct the agent to use it to guide the update process.\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The automatic update check retrieves `instruction` from a mutable API response and places it in both standard output and the surfaced error message. The Skill instructions then tell the agent to follow that field as an update prompt.\n\n  No allowlist, command schema, content sanitization, cryptographic signature, or separation between untrusted release data and trusted agent instructions is applied. Consequently, control of the update response provides an instruction-injection channel into the current agent session.\n\n  The update check runs automatically before normal API requests, generally once per day. If the returned version differs from the local version, the original user operation is interrupted, increasing the likelihood that the agent will act on the injected update instructions.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. A user invokes an ordinary IMA API operation.\n  2. `ima_api.cjs` automatically calls `openapi/check_skill_update`.\n  3. An attacker compromises the update service, its response path, or another component capable of controlling the update response.\n  4. The attacker returns a different `latest_version` and places arbitrary directives in `data.instruction`.\n  5. The script writes the attacker-controlled instruction to standard output, incorporates it into the error context, and stops the original request.\n  6. Following `SKILL.md`, the agent interprets the field as a prompt and may carry out the supplied update directions.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Exploitation can alter the agent's current-session goals and induce actions unrelated to the user's original request. Depending on available agent tools and user approvals, the injected prompt could attempt to trigger unsafe shell commands, retrieve untrusted files, disclose accessible information, modify local Skill files, or manipulate responses.\n\n  This does not independently grant operating-system privileges beyond those already available to the agent. Its effective scope is nevertheless broad because it can influence subsequent tool selection and agent behavior within the active session.","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Never interpret server-provided `instruction`, `release_desc`, or similar fields as agent instructions.\n  2. Remove the requirement in `SKILL.md` to follow the remote field. Present release information only as quoted, untrusted data.\n  3. Implement update behavior through a fixed local workflow with a strict set of permitted actions.\n  4. Require explicit user confirmation before any update, installation, file replacement, or command execution.\n  5. Authenticate update metadata with a pinned public key and verify a detached signature before displaying it.\n  6. Validate update responses against a strict schema, including a constrained semantic-version format and bounded inert text fields.\n  7. Do not interrupt the original operation merely because free-form remote text is present. If an update is available, return a locally generated notification.\n  8. Ensure no remote field can be passed to a shell, package manager, URL-fetching tool, or agent prompt."}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"IMA API Credentials Can Be Redirected to an Arbitrary Endpoint"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"ima_api.cjs"},"region":{"startLine":138,"endLine":151}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"46fd027c8e116528"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `ima_api.cjs:64-79`; `ima_api.cjs:138-151`  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Unrestricted credential-bearing API destination override  \n  **Risk Level**: High\n\n  ### Vulnerable Code\n\n  ```js\n  async function postJson(apiPath, body, requestOptions) {\n    const { clientId, apiKey, skillVersion, baseUrl } = requestOptions;\n\n    const res = await fetch(`${baseUrl}/${apiPath}`, {\n      method: 'POST',\n      headers: {\n        'ima-openapi-clientid': clientId,\n        'ima-openapi-apikey': apiKey,\n        'ima-openapi-ctx': `skill_version=${skillVersion}`,\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n      },\n      body: JSON.stringify(body),\n    });\n\n    return await res.text();\n  }\n  ```\n\n  ```js\n  async function imaApi(apiPath, body, options = {}) {\n    const forceCheck = options.forceCheck || options.forceUpdateCheck || process.env.IMA_FORCE_UPDATE_CHECK === '1';\n    const baseUrl = options.baseUrl || process.env.IMA_BASE_URL || DEFAULT_BASE_URL;\n    const lastCheckFile = options.lastCheckFile || process.env.IMA_LAST_CHECK_FILE || DEFAULT_LAST_CHECK_FILE;\n    const { clientId, apiKey } = loadCredentials(options);\n    const skillVersion = loadSkillVersion(options);\n\n    const requestOptions = {\n      forceCheck,\n      clientId,\n      apiKey,\n      skillVersion,\n      baseUrl,\n      lastCheckFile,\n    };\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The Skill documentation states that user credentials are sent only to `https://ima.qq.com`. The implementation does not enforce that restriction. Instead, `baseUrl` can be supplied through the caller-controlled options object or the `IMA_BASE_URL` environment variable.\n\n  Credentials are loaded independently from options, environment variables, or files under `~/.config/ima`. The selected Client ID and API key are then attached as HTTP headers to every request sent through the overridden `baseUrl`.\n\n  There is no URL parsing, HTTPS enforcement, exact-origin allowlist, hostname validation, or development-mode separation. A malicious or compromised launcher that can influence process options or environment variables can therefore redirect credential-bearing traffic away from the declared official API.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. The victim has valid IMA credentials in environment variables or under `~/.config/ima`.\n  2. An attacker influences the process environment or a caller of the exported `imaApi` function.\n  3. The attacker sets `IMA_BASE_URL` or `options.baseUrl` to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n  4. The user or agent invokes a normal notes or knowledge-base operation.\n  5. `loadCredentials()` retrieves the victim's credentials.\n  6. `postJson()` sends the Client ID and API key in HTTP headers to the substituted endpoint.\n  7. The attacker captures and reuses the credentials against the legitimate IMA API, subject to the permissions and limits assigned to those credentials.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation discloses the user's IMA Client ID and API key. An attacker could exercise all API permissions granted to those credentials, potentially including searching and reading private notes, enumerating knowledge bases, creating notes, irreversibly appending to existing notes, importing URLs, and initiating file-upload workflows.\n\n  The issue exceeds least privilege because a configuration override can silently broaden the credential destination from the documented official origin to an arbitrary host. Exploitation requires the ability to affect the process environment or API options, but those are common boundaries for launchers, wrappers, automation systems, and other loaded Skill instructions.","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Remove the `baseUrl` option and `IMA_BASE_URL` override from production builds.\n  2. Parse the destination with the standard `URL` class and require:\n     - protocol exactly `https:`;\n     - hostname exactly `ima.qq.com`;\n     - the expected port or no explicit port;\n     - no embedded username or password.\n  3. Construct API URLs from a constant trusted origin and validate `apiPath` as a relative allowlisted API path.\n  4. Configure redirects defensively. Reject any redirect to a different origin and never forward authentication headers across origins.\n  5. If endpoint overrides are required for testing, place them behind an explicit development mode that refuses to load credentials from production environment variables or `~/.config/ima`.\n  6. Use separate, non-production test credentials with narrowly scoped permissions for local testing.\n  7. Add automated tests proving that malicious origins, alternate ports, userinfo URLs, malformed hosts, and cross-origin redirects are rejected before credentials are loaded or transmitted.\n  8. Rotate potentially exposed API keys after deploying the corrected implementation."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":20,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789181776.4861743,"endTime":1789181885.3230698}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"ima-skill","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v574p4w1956kfqtr2vzdx72nt18e9wfh-o6iDWr/clawscan-skillspector-2629670828/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-12T02:56:15.761923+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":95,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":285,"executable":false,"size_bytes":15980,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"ima_api.cjs","type":"other","lines":226,"executable":true,"size_bytes":6390,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"knowledge-base/SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":383,"executable":false,"size_bytes":18095,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","type":"markdown","lines":595,"executable":false,"size_bytes":27034,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"knowledge-base/scripts/cos-upload.cjs","type":"other","lines":174,"executable":true,"size_bytes":5251,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"knowledge-base/scripts/preflight-check.cjs","type":"other","lines":313,"executable":true,"size_bytes":12074,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"meta.json","type":"json","lines":10,"executable":false,"size_bytes":236,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"notes/SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":191,"executable":false,"size_bytes":10762,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"notes/references/api.md","type":"markdown","lines":365,"executable":false,"size_bytes":16154,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-a933b2241c4c4d898588ac52634cdbd2","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill declares allowed domains in metadata, but it does not declare an explicit tool scope such as permissions or allowed-tools while requiring environment-variable access and outbound network access. In agent frameworks, missing explicit tool scoping can cause over-broad runtime capabilities or make policy enforcement ambiguous, increasing the chance that credentials or network actions are available in contexts the author did not narrowly constrain.","remediation":"Add explicit tool/permission declarations for the minimum required capabilities, e.g. environment access only for the two credential variables and network access only to the documented endpoints. Ensure the runtime enforces those scopes, and deny filesystem, shell, or other tools unless strictly necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-20bb2f69b1924eada02aecfced9e4ac5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.71,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":8},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language description and invocation guidance are written entirely around Chinese trigger phrases and Chinese user interactions, with no indication that the user may choose another language. This can amount to a locale/language constraint that is not explicitly documented as optional or region-specific.","remediation":"Document that the skill supports specific languages by design, or explicitly allow user language choice and provide equivalent triggers or guidance for other languages.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":8}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-7dd994273024411b9b6b69d2f61de0ad","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":5,"end_line":8},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger description is extremely broad and matches common phrases like '帮我记一下' or generic document-storage intents, which can cause the skill to activate for many unrelated requests. Over-broad activation increases the chance of unintended access to personal notes, knowledge-base data, or credentialed API actions without sufficiently clear user intent.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger phrases to explicit knowledge-base and IMA-specific intents, and require confirmation for ambiguous note-taking language. Add examples of non-matching phrases and a disambiguation step before any read/write action when user intent is unclear.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":5,"end_line":8}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-722861882c13417db9f4ce9853f67ceb","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":40,"end_line":null},"finding":"Do NOT ask user","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n1. **UTF-8 encoding (notes writes only):** Before calling `import_doc` or `append_doc`, ALL string fields (`content`, `title`) MUST be validated as legal UTF-8. Non-UTF-8 content causes irreversible garbled text. See [Detailed Rules](#detailed-utf-8-encoding-rules) for platform-specific methods.\n2. **File upload naming:** `title` MUST equal `file_name` (with extension). Never rename, shorten, translate, or modify the original filename.\n3. **Unsupported file types:** Reject immediately with a clear message. Do NOT ask user \"do you still want to try?\" Video files, Bilibili/YouTube URLs, and `file://` URLs are not supported — tell user to use IMA desktop client.\n4. **File upload integrity:** Keep file content as-is during upload. No encoding conversion for binary files (PDF, images, Excel, etc.).\n5. **PowerShell 5.1 (all modules):** If running in PowerShell, detect version before first API call. PS 5.1 silently converts request Body to GBK — must use UTF-8 byte array mode. See [Detailed Rules](#powershell-51-environment-detection).\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7a8fb39bcbe2d460cfca4f08109466a3d02622f82c750d24f19f1c0ef66a0a4c","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":40,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-a3ec91f95fba4142974878bacdea240f","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x83","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\n## 模块决策表\n\n| 用户意图                                                                                   | 模块           | 读取                      |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------- | ------------------------- |\n| 搜索笔记、浏览笔记本、获取笔记内容、创建笔记、追加内容                                     | notes          | `notes/SKILL.md`          |\n| 上传文件、添加网页链接、搜索知识库、浏览知识库内容、获取知识库信息、获取可添加的知识库列表 | knowledge-base | `knowledge-base/SKILL.md` |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"08e60b40ef57fe6a28ebd0c1d9364977dc48298c796c9b9f752b4efbfe67a779","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-a3ec91f95fba4142974878bacdea240f","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":66,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x83","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\n## 模块决策表\n\n| 用户意图                                                                                   | 模块           | 读取                      |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------- | ------------------------- |\n| 搜索笔记、浏览笔记本、获取笔记内容、创建笔记、追加内容                                     | notes          | `notes/SKILL.md`          |\n| 上传文件、添加网页链接、搜索知识库、浏览知识库内容、获取知识库信息、获取可添加的知识库列表 | knowledge-base | `knowledge-base/SKILL.md` |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"08e60b40ef57fe6a28ebd0c1d9364977dc48298c796c9b9f752b4efbfe67a779","occurrences":[{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":66,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-3771d3ce642a48f0a002f38489599a87","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":95,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.config/ima\necho \"your_client_id\" > ~/.config/ima/client_id\necho \"your_api_key\" > ~/.config","explanation":"The skill instructs users to persist API credentials in plaintext files under ~/.config/ima, which creates a local secret-at-rest exposure risk. If the host is multi-user, backed up insecurely, synced, or later accessed by another process, the credentials can be stolen and used to access the user's IMA account and data.","remediation":"Prefer secure secret storage mechanisms such as OS keychains, credential managers, or the agent platform's secret store. If file-based storage must be supported, require restrictive permissions (e.g. 600), clearly document the risk, avoid echoing secrets in shell history, and prefer reading credentials from protected environment injection rather than writing plaintext files.","code_snippet":"**方式 A — 配置文件（推荐）：**\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.config/ima\necho \"your_client_id\" > ~/.config/ima/client_id\necho \"your_api_key\" > ~/.config/ima/api_key\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"fddbf84bc24b7153a5798922bbcd7a4044a96af31a75695348568ead898160fe","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":95,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-36c46f048ff64c8d99326169c5418b2a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":28,"end_line":48},"finding":null,"explanation":"This function accesses API credentials from environment variables and files under ~/.config/ima, which is sensitive data handling. The file does not include a user-facing warning, confirmation, or explanatory comment describing that credential sources will be read.","remediation":"Document in code comments, docstrings, or user-visible output that the skill loads credentials from specific environment variables and config files. If appropriate, provide a startup notice indicating which credential source is being used without exposing the secret values.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":28,"end_line":48}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f0d1427baf2f43b593d4a7e504f42361","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":64,"end_line":76},"finding":null,"explanation":"The helper sends API credentials in headers and transmits the provided request body to a remote service via fetch, but there is no confirmation prompt, logging, or explanatory comment/docstring warning users that data will be sent off-host. For a generic API wrapper, this outbound transmission is safety-relevant and not disclosed within the file.","remediation":"Add a clear user-facing disclosure or comment/docstring stating that the function sends the request body and authentication headers to the remote IMA API endpoint. If used interactively, consider printing/logging the destination and nature of the transmission before sending.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":64,"end_line":76}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-1b1661dacfa249be9c50db72418bdfb0","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"knowledge-base/SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x91","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\n## 接口决策表\n\n| 用户意图                                      | 调用接口                                                               | 关键参数                                                                                           |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 上传文件到知识库                              | `check_repeated_names` → `create_media` → COS Upload → `add_knowledge` | `media_type`（按扩展名），`knowledge_base_id`，`file_name`，`file_size`                    