 ID）                   | 见「文件夹操作」章节                                                                               |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f9dae145ce157b04d98cb044b7211be0641900f77eed697377edbe1a34fb51ac","occurrences":[{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":154,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c44ad6a3600542db897b924564079828","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":12,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation instructs users to include long-lived API keys in headers and later exposes temporary COS credentials, but it does not warn that these values are secrets that must not be logged, embedded in client-side code, or disclosed to end users. In a skill/integration context, omission of secret-handling guidance can lead implementers to leak credentials through prompts, traces, browser requests, or debugging output, enabling unauthorized API or storage access.","remediation":"Add explicit secret-handling guidance near the authentication and COS credential sections: store secrets only in server-side secret management, never print or return them to users, redact them from logs, and scope/expire temporary credentials as tightly as possible. Also document that clientid/apikey and COS temporary credentials must only be used in trusted backend flows, with rotation and revocation procedures.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":12,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-af8211c6f5254317bac2450e2df2583b","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":156,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x93","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\n| 值  | 名称           | content_type / 说明                                                                                           |\n| --- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1   | PDF            | `application/pdf`                                                                                             |\n| 2   | 网页           | N/A（直接 AddKnowledge，`web_info.content_id=<url>`）                                                         |\n| 3   | Word           | `application/msword` / `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document`              |\n| 4   | PPT            | `application/vnd.ms-powerpoint` / `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation` |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"43be23ee112b3e118fb7aa7983fccadd0c25310b114941bfe5d48a5ef0f703c5","occurrences":[{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":156,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-1e86ab8225b64371b3da32d7cd0b960b","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":166,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x98","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"| 9   | 图片           | `image/png`, `image/jpeg`, `image/webp`                                                                       |\n| 11  | 笔记           | N/A（直接 AddKnowledge，`note_info.content_id=<doc_id>`）                                                     |\n| 12  | AI会话         | N/A（直接 AddKnowledge，`session_info.content_id=<session_id>`）                                              |\n| 13  | TXT            | `text/plain`                                                                                                  |\n| 14  | Xmind          | `application/x-xmind` / `application/vnd.xmind.workbook` / `application/zip`                                  |\n| 15  | 录音           | `audio/mpeg`(mp3), `audio/x-m4a`(m4a), `audio/wav`(wav), `audio/aac`(aac)                                     |\n| 16  | 视频解析       | **不支持通过 skill 添加**。Bilibili/YouTube/本地HTML等仅支持在 ima 桌面端内添加进知识库                       |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e67553727c1229c6de1adf40cdf3fa28d6005dd8db4aa82e57f9095a9897ef2a","occurrences":[{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":166,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-e9dc788f3fca4f62a333b6d739a20cea","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":467,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x94","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\n#### 返回字段（`data` 内）\n\n| 字段                | 类型            | 说明                                                                                              |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `media_type`        | int32           | 媒体类型（见 MediaType 枚举）                                                                     |\n| `url_info`          | URLInfo         | 访问链接信息，非笔记类型时填写（见 [URLInfo](#urlinfo访问链接信息)）                              |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"fe436e6ebb49a4bf15ff765f2ba6499abf022d5785f98bc91efdc9900a76c8fb","occurrences":[{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":467,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4c1ac85db4994b2a86f50dd210ccc2d9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":475,"end_line":479},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document directs the consumer to request returned URLs together with supplied headers, but does not warn that those headers may contain bearer tokens or other authorization material for protected content. In an agent skill, blindly replaying server-provided URLs and headers can cause credential forwarding to untrusted destinations, SSRF-like behavior, or unintended access to sensitive documents.","remediation":"Add a security warning before this flow: treat returned URLs and headers as sensitive, only fetch from allowlisted domains, never forward authorization headers across domain boundaries, and strip or redact secrets from logs and user-visible output. Require validation of scheme/host, enforce backend-only retrieval, and document that protected-content fetches should use least-privilege tokens with short expiry.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","start_line":475,"end_line":479}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-85606f88134a4affa2bb648e06e75480","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":7,"end_line":12},"finding":null,"explanation":"The authentication section instructs clients to send a client ID and API key but does not explicitly warn that these are secrets that must never be exposed in prompts, logs, examples, or user-visible output. For agent-integrated skills, missing secret-handling guidance increases the chance of credential leakage through debugging, error messages, or prompt injection side effects.","remediation":"Add explicit secret-handling requirements: never echo credentials, never place them in user-controlled content, redact them from logs, and store them only in secure secret management systems. Include guidance for rotating compromised keys and handling auth failures without revealing sensitive values.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":7,"end_line":12}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-2338f39cf256458bb7ee3212a29a30f2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":216,"end_line":216},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger guidance uses broad natural-language phrases such as generic 'search/find notes' patterns, which can cause the skill to activate when the user did not intend to access private note data. In a privacy-sensitive notes context, accidental invocation can lead to unnecessary retrieval of notebooks, note metadata, or contents.","remediation":"Tighten activation criteria to require explicit notebook/note intent and, for content access, explicit confirmation of which note to search or open. Add disambiguation prompts when user language could refer to general chat memory, web search, or non-note tasks.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":216,"end_line":216}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f8a6b52eb3064aadb35d1643378faf3d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":247,"end_line":266},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation describes create and append behaviors but does not clearly warn that these actions modify persistent user data. In a privacy-focused notes skill, insufficient disclosure raises the risk of users unknowingly causing durable writes, which can expose, retain, or alter sensitive information beyond the current conversation.","remediation":"Add prominent warnings in the write-operation sections that these actions create or modify stored notes. Require the agent workflow to surface a brief confirmation before execution and log write actions distinctly from read-only operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":247,"end_line":266}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-a9f5950ed9984d328c2738d63cfcc6fe","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":251,"end_line":251},"finding":null,"explanation":"The create-note trigger description includes broad phrases like saving content as a note without requiring a clear write-intent confirmation. That increases the chance of unintended persistent data creation, which is a user-data integrity and privacy issue because conversation content may be stored durably without sufficient user awareness.","remediation":"Require explicit user consent before any create/import action, using confirmation language that clearly states a new note will be created and saved. Restrict trigger phrases to unambiguous write intents such as 'create a note' or 'save this to my notes,' and avoid implicit persistence from casual conversation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":251,"end_line":251}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-7b7e74beb5eb4a69a378cba03a51d21b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":262,"end_line":262},"finding":null,"explanation":"Appending to an existing note is a state-changing operation, and the trigger guidance does not impose strict enough conditions before performing that write. In a note-management skill, accidental append operations can silently alter user records, corrupt note contents, or add sensitive chat material to the wrong note.","remediation":"Gate append operations behind explicit write-intent plus note disambiguation and user confirmation, especially when multiple candidate notes exist. Update the documentation to state that append actions modify stored user data and should only run after clear authorization.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"notes/references/api.md","start_line":262,"end_line":262}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-df0bbf9997804ce891dfd3415c4ecb05","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":44,"end_line":44},"finding":null,"explanation":"The error message text is hard-coded in Chinese, and similar Chinese-only messages appear elsewhere in the file. Because the skill does not offer language selection or justify a Chinese-only locale requirement, this is a natural-language locale policy concern.","remediation":"Provide localized messages based on user preference or environment, or document that the skill is intentionally Chinese-only for a justified region-specific use case.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":44,"end_line":44}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-5ba9bc22780b440c9eae6271ccfbf54d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":90,"end_line":137},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes a unified IMA OpenAPI skill for note management and knowledge-base actions such as upload, search, browse, create, and edit. This code additionally performs a daily version-update check against a separate endpoint and writes update-check state to a local file, which is an operational capability not justified by the user-facing skill purpose.","remediation":"Remove the automatic update-check behavior from the skill runtime, or explicitly declare this maintenance capability in the manifest/documentation. If retained, isolate it from normal request handling and document its network and file-write side effects clearly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":90,"end_line":137}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-10e42641ba454db4b72d799a48f9ad51","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":170,"end_line":170},"finding":null,"explanation":"This user-visible parse error message is emitted only in Chinese, which forces a specific language for users regardless of their locale. No opt-in or documented locale restriction is present in the file.","remediation":"Add localization support or a documented language-selection mechanism, such as choosing messages from LANG/LC_ALL or an explicit option.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":170,"end_line":170}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-2ae32cdd7608402191be96dccdd21f29","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":184,"end_line":184},"finding":null,"explanation":"The options parsing error shown to users is only available in Chinese. This enforces a language choice without opt-in or justification.","remediation":"Localize CLI messages or document a clear, justified Chinese-only scope for this skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":184,"end_line":184}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-d13c1846d7404df194ee8fea577c0db0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":200,"end_line":212},"finding":null,"explanation":"The missing-argument and unknown-error messages presented to users are Chinese-only. Since the file does not provide multilingual support or explain a region-specific constraint, this is a language policy issue.","remediation":"Offer translated messages or select message language based on user configuration or environment; alternatively, document a justified locale restriction.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"ima_api.cjs","start_line":200,"end_line":212}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-54474d94b35f413b9f490d4e36c4ce13","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","co